 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Fuzzy Metaballs](7316-fuzzy-metaballs.md)
-Fuzzy Metaballs is an algebraic, implicit surface representation that defines geometry as the zero level set of a function composed of multidimensional Gaussians (ellipsoids) rather than isotropic ones. It serves as the foundational object representation for differentiable rendering pipelines, enabling robust optimization by relaxing hard thresholds to ensure smooth gradients during ray-tracing. Unlike Weighted Blending, which focuses on sort-free image-order rendering, Fuzzy Metaballs provides the underlying implicit field definition that allows for the computation of surface normals and distance-based losses. [Fuzzy Metaballs](7316-fuzzy-metaballs.md)
